title two proofs of one promise -- the Constel naming law read both ways, and the number where they part
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure-Glow lane.
think ListAgents at open named one peer, grain-a2, interactive, nine hours old. The %291 law says name it before a file moves, so it is named here and it mattered: nine tracked files I never touched appeared in the working tree during my cold roster, and the roster closed with tree_moved=yes for exactly that reason.
think Rota N read at the open. git rev-list --count HEAD gave 3595, and 3595 mod 5 is 0 -- Aether, which is the row the last recorded lap read at N=3545. A repeat, so advanced by hand to row 1: Air and Saturn, law and boundary, whose sense is touch. Threshold, TAME Core, Single-Stranded, Gauge. The sentence carried out of it: you check whether a part stands free by trying to pull it out, and a boundary the hand passes through was a wish.
think That is what the lap then did, to a boundary nobody had pressed. The Glow-tree charter booked two defects on 20260827 and left them; the first (a witness calling a python3 path that became .rish) is already repaired. The second was live: constel/name.rye admits a fake-pier name only when it is vowel-free, while tools/fixtures/constel_naming_scan.sh checked the elder digit property from a day earlier.
think Pulling on it found a third site the charter did not name. pond/apps/constel_net.rye:49 mirrors the law a second time in Rye and checks the digit, and its own doc comment claims to be "exactly the check tools/fixtures/constel_naming_scan.sh runs". So one promise stands proven three times, in three rooms, and the three do not agree: all five names in the seated fixture carry vowels, and constel/handshake.rye:117 calls check_ship at its border, so it would refuse every name the Pond harness uses.
think Measured rather than assumed, twice. The first count of carrier modules read eleven from an eyeball of a grep listing; grepping all five names against pond/apps and tools/fixtures read ten modules and two Bron fixtures. The draft said eleven in three places before the measurement corrected it.
think The repair had to fit the lane. Rewriting Pond is Hush's, rewriting constel/ is Dream's, and neither is mine. What is mine is tools/, so the shape became the one this tree already uses for %303 and %304: build the guard that reads both sets, gate the safety union so the promise never weakens, and report the disagreement as a number. verdict now fires only when a name is safe by NEITHER proof, which is why every assertion the elder witness made still passes unchanged, including first=sarlev.
think Writing the fault fixture caught a bug in the repair itself. check_constellation walks i to whole.len inclusive, so a trailing hyphen yields one more empty segment and refuses BadSegment; my shell loop stopped at the last non-empty remainder and admitted "xnkg-" silently. The planted fixture found it in one run. A welcome proven as hard as a refusal is what makes the refusal mean something, and here it was the welcome fixture that proved the refusal wrong.
obs The roster ran 32 minutes and closed run_verdict=guard_red, 69 of 74 green, tree_moved=yes. Five reds, and sorting them by owner was most of the reds-first work: sow (IDENT_LEAK on seed/.git/config) is the peer's own in-flight repair, named in their publish-seed diff; declared_ceiling is REDS %295, OPEN and gated on Keaton's word; radiant_negation and prose_register both red against HEAD in a throwaway `git archive` pen, so neither is the peer's.
obs prose_register named one file: lotus/README.md at 27% negative against a 20% Door ceiling. Three sentences repaired, register only -- "stopped being written at ALES214" became "carries its last entry at ALES214", and the compressor lesson became "drifts quietly, because it keeps looking exactly as it did the day it was true". It reads 13% (3 of 22) and the scan says door_over_ceiling=0. CLAIM_PRESERVE_FILES=lotus/README.md proves tokens, modality, pins, and structure identical -- and running that witness unscoped reds by design, which cost one wrong reading before the message was read.
obs radiant_negation is left standing and surfaced rather than taken. Its three RISEN files are .claude/rules/checkpoint.md, lindy-first-crux.md and quin.md, and the peer is live in .claude/rules/ with three files of their own staged there. Editing that directory beside them is how %291 happens, so the honest move was to measure it, prove it pre-existing, and say so.
obs The REDS pin has no room left. Four rows stand and all four read OPEN, so tools/fixtures/reds_fold.sh lawfully refuses to move any of them, and 913 bytes was the whole allowance for a new row. %306 was written to 903 bytes against a house average of 2,966 -- five iterations of compression to fit. That is a structural fact worth Keaton's eye rather than a red: the ledger cannot hold its own live work under 24,576, which is the same arithmetic that raised session-logs/README.md's own bound on his word.
obs Not repaired, and named instead: foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md, read on the rota, banners itself "a Gauge reimagining of 20260823-204456_single-stranded.md, which stays whole as the fossil" -- a link to itself, for an elder (20260618-182412) that 3778c3d2d deleted. The QA card reads A+ 98 and truth_counted=100, because a self-citation resolves perfectly. It is dated testimony, so it takes an erratum rather than a quiet edit.
obs The six work files of this lap are committed under someone else's message. At 00:22:27 the peer ran what reads as git add -A and landed c6df347dd3 -- a crashed-meteor commit whose body names no Constel and no lotus -- carrying constel_naming_scan.sh, constel_naming_witness.rish, the three new fixtures, and lotus/README.md with it. It was pushed to xy and debrided before I read it, so it is shared and immutable, and accrete is the only lawful answer as well as the right one: this commit carries the ledger row, the card, and this log, and its body says where the tool files actually went.
obs Two things went right inside that. The exec bit held -- constel_naming_scan.sh reads 100755 in the index, because the rewrite went through the original inode (cat tmp > file) per the exec-bit law, so a foreign add -A carried the mode instead of dropping it. And nothing broken rode in: constel_naming_witness, constel_net_witness, prose_register, and claim_preserve scoped to lotus/README.md were all GREEN on metal before the sweep took them.
obs This is REDS %291 firing a third way, and it could not be booked. The first firing was two hands doing one lap; %295 was one host leaving work another could not hold; this is one hand's add -A committing another hand's in-flight work under the wrong message -- and the repair an agent can make without Keaton is the same each time, stage path-limited. It is recorded here rather than in the ledger because construction/REDS.md stands at 24,569 of 24,576 with four OPEN rows, and reds_fold.sh lawfully refuses to move an OPEN row. The ledger has no room for the next red, which is the seat this lap hands up.
